<section>
<h2>24. Week 5 Reflection</h2>

<p>
This week helped me understand how information can be hidden
in different digital files, including images, PDFs and network
traffic. I learned that steganography hides the existence
of information, while cryptography protects information by
making it unreadable without the correct key.
</p>

<p>
I also learned about Least Significant Bit (LSB) image
steganography, PDF structures, metadata analysis, statistical
analysis and dynamic analysis. These techniques are important
because hidden information may create security risks when
files are shared through cloud services.
</p>

<p>
The practical activities helped me understand Caesar cipher
decoding, Base64 encoding, image steganography and PDF
investigation. I also learned how file hashes can be used
to check integrity and how detection metrics help evaluate
security systems.
</p>

<p>
The cloud security activities helped me understand the
importance of access control, Data Loss Prevention, CASB,
endpoint monitoring and audit logs. I learned that suspicious
activity should be investigated using evidence rather than
assumptions.
</p>

<p>
My main learning point is that one security tool is not
enough. Organisations need multiple layers of protection
and careful investigation to protect their information.
</p>

